From de4a058734a5aee1970abfed710c5b55afa8496d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NikoMalik <NikoMalik@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 11:50:42 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] lz4kdr: drop the hash table insert after every match

after each match the encoder hashed the last byte of the match into
ht[],perf annotate puts that load and multiply at about 12% of
encode_fast,and in a 1024-entry table the insert mostly evicts entries
the probe loop would have matched later,so heap pages get smaller
without it

the format is unchanged,hash() has no other user and goes away too


  python heap    18717358 -> 18360960  -1.9%   12762 12940 -> 12307 12323
  machine code   44670152 -> 44776403  +0.24%  18233 18448 -> 18024 17947
  text           11493417 -> 11570676  +0.67%  22799 22906 -> 22463 22433
  compressed     20864374 -> 20858281          2172  2178  -> 2211  2202
  all            95.74 MB -> 95.57 MB  -0.19%

zram holds mostly anonymous memory,which the heap set stands for

every page round trips,the test suite passes under asan and ubsan
---
 lib/lz4kdr/lz4kdr_encode.c | 19 +++++++------------
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/lib/lz4kdr/lz4kdr_encode.c b/lib/lz4kdr/lz4kdr_encode.c
index 4fc58a90cd94..b2766cacf581 100644
--- a/lib/lz4kdr/lz4kdr_encode.c
+++ b/lib/lz4kdr/lz4kdr_encode.c
@@ -403,13 +403,6 @@ const uint8_t *lz4kdr_repeat_end(
 	return repeat_end(q, r, in_end_safe, in_end);
 }
 
-/* CR increase order: +STEP, have OFFSETS, use _5b(most impact) */
-/* *_6b to compete with LZ4 */
-inline static uint_fast32_t hash(const uint8_t *r)
-{
-	return hash64_5b(r, HT_LOG2);
-}
-
 /*
  * Proof that 'r' increments are safe-NO pointer overflows are possible:
  *
@@ -473,10 +466,7 @@ static int encode_any(
 			 * (v>>8)'s low 5 bytes = r[1..6) hash position r+1 --
 			 * one load instead of two, and both ht[] loads/hashes
 			 * can issue back to back instead of waiting on the
-			 * first equal4pv(). This bypasses hash()/hashed()
-			 * entirely for the probe loop; hash() is still used
-			 * once per match below (ht[hash(r - 1)]), just far
-			 * less often than it was called here.
+			 * first equal4pv(). This bypasses hashed() entirely.
 			 */
 			{
 				const uint64_t v = read8_at(r);
@@ -511,7 +501,12 @@ static int encode_any(
 		if (unlikely((r += r_bytes_max) > in_end_safe))
 			return out_tail2(out_at, out_end, out, r, in_end,
 					 NR_LOG2, OFF_LOG2);
-		ht[hash(r - 1)] = (uint16_t)(r - 1 - in0);
+		/*
+		 * No ht[] insert for the last byte of the match: in a
+		 * 1024-entry table it mostly evicts entries the probe loop
+		 * would have found, and its extra load and multiply cost
+		 * about 12% of the encoder.
+		 */
 	}
 }
 
